Original code: `if (data && Array.isArray(data.nodes)) return data.nodes;` — the path lookup for ['nodes'] returns data.nodes (the array itself), and the original checked Array.isArray(rt.nodes) where rt was the HOLDER. My envelopeNodesAt treats the path result as the holder. Fix: make envelopeNodesAt check whether the resolved value is itself an array OR has a .nodes array:

```javascript
